From 471ae1aebf6f5d84cd04168dbc334a5b52817010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordi <jordi@exante.ai>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 18:51:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app): ground pets on a shared contact line, idle
 stays at work zone, re-push zone swaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- viewSignature now includes workKind, so a read→edit zone swap with unchanged liveness
  re-pushes the scene (PixiStage keys its showAll effect on the signature) — previously the
  boulder→tree swap was silently dropped.
- Per-body feet alignment to a shared GROUND_Y: measured the worker body's feet at a constant
  0.75 across every pose (so chopping no longer jumps), knight at 1.0; the player renders
  smaller (0.72) with its own feet line. Floor pad restored to the original near-square size;
  scene prop back on the floor.
- Pets stay at their work zone when idle (stand by the activity) instead of walking to camp;
  the daemon keeps the work-kind sticky between turns.
- Lumber (tree-chopping) now stands on grass, not a sawmill floor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
